content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-113 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22650",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is reported as 4.8 mm/s. Figure 3 applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported reading meets those measurement conditions, 4.8 is between the 4.5 and 7.1 mm/s RMS boundaries and therefore falls in Zone C: 'Restricted - plan maintenance.' It is not in Zone D, so this reading does not trigger the immediate-stop rule. Classification remains provisional until RMS measurement and the non-drive-end reading are confirmed, because the highest reading on either bearing housing must be used.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable documented temperature limits are specifically for the bearing housing: normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. If the reported 'Housing 70 C' is the bearing-housing temperature, it is exactly at the upper normal limit, below both alarm and trip. It is not above the manufacturer's alarm limit, so the requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered by temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage is reported, so the report does not document the manual's 'leakage at shaft seal' symptom. The current evidence therefore does not justify seal replacement on leakage grounds; seal work should remain conditional on inspection or another identified need.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: shaft misalignment following motor replacement. The high-vibration troubleshooting entry lists misalignment first among several possible causes, and the manual requires laser alignment after work that moves the motor or bearing housing. The timing after the motor replacement and restart makes this the first check.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear is another documented cause of high vibration and high bearing temperature. It is not proven by the present readings: 70 C is still at the normal upper limit if measured on the bearing housing. Inspect both bearings and replace them as a pair only if either shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage remains a documented possible cause if alignment and bearing condition do not explain the vibration; inspect the impeller during any resulting internal inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation is also a documented possible cause. Check NPSH if vibration persists after alignment or if inspection/operating symptoms indicate cavitation; the evidence provides no NPSH value with which to assess it now.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "At the maintenance visit, verify the drive-end reading as vibration velocity in mm/s RMS on the bearing housing, measure the non-drive-end bearing housing as well, and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Also confirm the location of the 70 C housing-temperature measurement. Restore the specified weekly two-housing vibration checks after maintenance.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Review the electrical contractor's motor-replacement and any alignment records. Perform laser shaft alignment following the motor replacement, and correct alignment to parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After alignment, remeasure vibration and bearing-housing temperature. If high vibration persists, inspect the bearings and impeller and check NPSH to distinguish bearing wear, impeller imbalance/damage and cavitation. If high bearing temperature is subsequently confirmed, also check grease quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any internal pump or seal work, implement the isolation, line-break and lifting controls listed in safety_controls. Drain and vent before line break; use the planned certified lift for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly if that assembly is removed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection finds wear, noise or high temperature in either bearing, replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Do not replace them solely because the reported temperature is 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing has been opened. For fasteners actually disturbed, use Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm and bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm. The seal-gland torque is governed by the serial-specific bulletin in the next step, not by the manual's general 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if seal replacement is separately justified or added after inspection, follow procedure 5.2: isolate and drain; remove the back pull-out assembly; remove the impeller nut and impeller; withdraw the seal and sleeve and inspect the sleeve for scoring; fit the new seal and a new casing gasket. For this serial, fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed for seal setting, and tighten its gland nuts to 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry. Verify vibration on both bearing housings and bearing-housing temperature, and classify the highest vibration reading. If a reading falls in Zone D, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart; if bearing temperature rises above the 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity one. Conditional on opening the casing; it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened and is also required during seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Conditional supply only if bearing inspection requires replacement; replace together with HF3-510 as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Conditional supply only if bearing inspection requires replacement; replace together with HF3-512 as a pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal. Conditional only if seal replacement is added; this is the required replacement for the superseded HF3-450 on this serial-range pump. Do not fit HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Conditional on seal work and inspection finding scoring deeper than 0.1 mm; no replacement need is established by the current report.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg threshold. Before lifting it, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration is provisionally Zone C, not the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so immediate stopping is not presently mandated. If the highest confirmed reading falls in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are mandatory if the work is on a chemically dosed line. The specific sodium-hypochlorite dosing note identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, not P-113; confirm P-113's actual service before line break rather than assuming whether this conditional PPE applies.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: allow the standard 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement as a pair, only if inspection requires it: allow the standard 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement, only if added to scope after inspection: allow the standard 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts table lists component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and specifies cartridge HF3-450B with 30 Nm gland torque for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-113 is serial HF3-22650 and therefore lies inside that range, so the bulletin governs any seal work on this asset: use HF3-450B at 30 Nm, not HF3-450 at 25 Nm. The bulletin also states that pre-set HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement for seal setting, while scoring deeper than 0.1 mm requires sleeve replacement. This resolution does not itself establish that seal replacement is currently necessary.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Was the 4.8 mm/s drive-end reading an RMS velocity measured on the bearing housing, and what is the non-drive-end reading? Both are needed to confirm the Figure 3 classification using the highest reading.",
    "Is the reported 70 C temperature specifically the bearing-housing temperature? The normal, alarm and trip limits in C02 apply to that location.",
    "What were the as-found parallel and angular alignment values, and did the electrical contractor record or perform a post-replacement laser alignment?",
    "What are the bearing noise/condition and grease findings, impeller condition, and suction/NPSH data? These are needed to establish the root cause and decide whether the conditional bearings, seal or sleeve are actually required.",
    "Is P-113 installed on any chemically dosed line? C16 explicitly identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line but does not describe P-113's service, so the applicability of chemical goggles and nitrile gloves must be confirmed before line break.",
    "How long can this specific pump remain in restricted Zone C service before the planned repair, and what completion date is required? The supplied documents require maintenance to be planned but give no maximum Zone C run time.",
    "What labour should be allowed for diagnostic inspection and NPSH checking? Table 6 supplies standard times for alignment, bearing replacement and seal replacement, but not for those diagnostic tasks."
  ]
}
